.TH APG 1 "October 15, 2026" "apg" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apg \- Advanced Password Generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apg
[\fB\-a\fR \fI0|1\fR]
[\fB\-M\fR \fImode\fR]
[\fB\-E\fR \fIchars\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR \fIcount\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fImin\fR]
[\fB\-x\fR \fImax\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-\-length\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-strategy\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-alnum\fR]
[\fB\-\-pin\fR]
[\fB\-C\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apg
generates strong passwords: random ones or pronounceable ones built with the
FIPS-181 algorithm. Its options follow the classic apg (Automated Password
Generator) by Adel I. Mirzazhanov, with a few extensions.
.PP
Without options apg prints one random 32-character password made of upper and
lower case letters, digits and special characters. Every random choice comes
from the operating system's cryptographic random generator.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options of the classic apg
.TP
.BI \-a " 0|1"
Algorithm: 0 builds pronounceable passwords (FIPS-181), 1 picks random
characters. Default: 1.
.TP
.BI \-M " mode"
Symbol classes to use:
.B S
special symbols,
.B N
numbers,
.B C
capital letters,
.B L
small letters. An upper case letter means every password must contain the
class, a lower case letter means it may. Default: SNCL.
.TP
.BI \-E " chars"
Exclude these characters, for example look-alikes such as
.BR O0Il1| .
.TP
.BI \-n " count"
Number of passwords to generate. Default: 1.
.TP
.BI \-m " min"
Minimum password length. Default: 32.
.TP
.BI \-x " max"
Maximum password length. Default: 32. If it is less than the minimum, the
minimum is used.
.TP
.BI \-r " file"
Reject passwords found in a dictionary file, one word per line.
.TP
.B \-t
Print the pronunciation of pronounceable passwords.
.TP
.B \-l
Spell out generated passwords, for example
.B aB1!
as
.BR alfa-Bravo-ONE-EXCLAMATION_POINT .
.TP
.B \-d
Do not print a newline after each password.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode: do not print warnings.
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-c " seed"
Random seed options. Accepted for compatibility and ignored.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.SS Extensions
.TP
.BI \-\-length " N"
Exact password length, same as
.BI \-m " N " \-x " N" .
.TP
.BI \-\-strategy " name"
.B full
(\-M SNCL),
.B alphanum
(\-M NCL) or
.B digits
(\-M N).
.TP
.B \-\-alnum
Same as
.BR "\-\-strategy alphanum" .
.TP
.BR \-\-digits ", " \-\-pin
Same as
.BR "\-\-strategy digits" ,
for PIN codes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-newline
Same as
.BR \-d .
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-copy
Copy the generated passwords to the clipboard with pbcopy (macOS), clip
(Windows), or wl-copy, xclip or xsel (Linux).
.PP
When several strategy or
.B \-M
options are given, the last one wins. Short options cannot be combined:
write
.BR "\-d \-l" ,
not
.BR \-dl .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.apg.conf
Default settings, one
.I key=value
per line; blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Command-line
options take precedence.
.RS
.TP
.BI default_length= N
Password length when no length option is given.
.TP
.BI default_strategy= name
.BR full ,
.B alphanum
or
.BR digits .
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if passwords could not be generated or copied, 2 on invalid
options or configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B apg
One random 32-character password.
.TP
.B apg \-a 0 \-n 6 \-m 8 \-x 10 \-M sncl
Six pronounceable passwords, like the classic apg prints by default.
.TP
.B apg \-\-pin \-\-length 6
A six-digit PIN code.
.TP
.B apg \-E 'O0Il1|' \-\-length 16 \-C
A 16-character password without look-alike characters, copied to the
clipboard.
.TP
.B apg \-d | pbcopy
A password without a trailing newline.
.SH DIFFERENCES FROM THE CLASSIC APG
Defaults differ (see above). Bloom filter checks
.RB ( \-b ", " \-p ),
crypt(3) output
.RB ( \-y )
and cracklib checks
.RB ( \-k )
are not supported; apg exits with an error instead of skipping a check.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/eslusarenko/apg
